        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=12$, so $y=12x$. Completed $y$ row: $0,12,24,36$.",
          "worked": "Since $y\\propto x$, $y=kx$. Using $(x,y)=(1,12)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}12&=k\\times1\\\\k&=12\\\\y&=12x\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x=2$, $y=12\\times2=24$. For $x=3$, $y=12\\times3=36$.\nThe completed $y$ row is $0,12,24,36$.",
