        "answer": {
          "short": "$k=1.5$, so $y=1.5x$. Completed $y$ row: $3,12,18,27$.",
          "worked": "Since $y\\propto x$, $y=kx$. Using $(x,y)=(2,3)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3&=2k\\\\k&=\\frac32\\\\y&=\\frac32x\\end{align*}$$\nFor $x=8$, $y=\\frac32\\times8=12$.\nFor $x=12$, $y=\\frac32\\times12=18$.\nFor $x=18$, $y=\\frac32\\times18=27$.\nThe completed $y$ row is $3,12,18,27$.",
